ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution:} Solve by combining the two function expressions, 
\[
\begin{cases}
y=2x+4\\ 
y=\frac{6}{x}
\end{cases}
\]
, and find $x_{1}=-3$, $x_{2}=1$ (discard $x_{2}$).\\
When $x=-3$, $y=2\times(-3)+4=-2$,\\
$\therefore$ the coordinates of point D are $\boxed{(-3, -2)}$.

